The static validation is clean, but we still need a live PostgreSQL execution test to verify:

every migration actually executes successfully,
every trigger compiles,
every constraint behaves as intended,
pg_trgm/extensions are available,
the vector configuration works,
the seed/bootstrap process works,
the immutable-event enforcement works at runtime.

After that live test, we can freeze V001 and proceed migration-by-migration from an actual database rather than continuing to design blindly.
